title: Select like a strategy game
intro: Selection Controls on the camera and a Selectable on each worker and machine: click, box, double-click, control groups and Esc, with no code.

project: Empty | Selection

chapter: Workers and a machine | A Selectable on each
create: Sprite
rename: Worker
set: Transform.Position.X = -3
set: Sprite.Tint = #57A0D3
add: Selectable
set: Selectable.Kind = Worker
explain: component:Selectable | Selectable | A Selectable makes this worker something the player can select with the mouse.
explain: field:Selectable.Kind | Kind | Its kind is what a double-click picks every one of.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Worker 2
set: Transform.Position.X = 3
set: Sprite.Tint = #57A0D3
add: Selectable
set: Selectable.Kind = Worker
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Worker 3
set: Transform.Position.Y = 3
set: Sprite.Tint = #57A0D3
add: Selectable
set: Selectable.Kind = Worker
say: Three workers.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Reader
set: Sprite.Size = 1.5, 1.5
set: Sprite.Tint = #D3A057
add: Selectable
set: Selectable.Kind = Reader
set: Selectable.InBox = false
explain: field:Selectable.InBox | In Box | And a machine between two of them. Its In Box is off, so a box drawn over the workers picks only them; a click still picks the machine.

chapter: The controls | Selection Controls on the camera
deselect
select: Main Camera
add: SelectionControls
explain: component:SelectionControls | Selection Controls | Selection Controls on the camera does the selecting: click, drag a box, Shift to add, double-click for every one of a kind, and Control with a number for groups.
set: SelectionControls.DoubleClickSeconds = 1
explain: field:SelectionControls.DoubleClickSeconds | Double Click Seconds | A double-click has to come this quickly. A second here, so the demo's mouse keeps up.
explain: field:SelectionControls.MarkerColor | Markers | A marker goes round each thing selected: an outline in this color, or a picture of your own, nine-sliced to fit.
explain: field:SelectionControls.BusyFlag | Busy | And while a tool is in hand, a flag or a script's Busy leaves the mouse to it.

chapter: Play | Box, double-click, groups and Esc
play
wait: 0.5
gamedrag: -4, -1.5, 4, 1.5
expectvalue: Main Camera.SelectionControls.SelectedCount = 2
say: A box over the bottom row picks the two workers and not the machine between them.
gameclick: Reader
expectvalue: Main Camera.SelectionControls.SelectedCount = 1
say: A click picks the machine on its own.
gameclick: Worker 3
gameclick: Worker 3
expectvalue: Main Camera.SelectionControls.SelectedCount = 3
say: A double-click on a worker picks every worker on screen.
hold: LeftControl+D2 0.2
tap: Escape
expectvalue: Main Camera.SelectionControls.SelectedCount = 0
say: Control and 2 keeps them as group two, and Escape clears the selection.
tap: D2
expectvalue: Main Camera.SelectionControls.SelectedCount = 3
tap: D2
expectat: Main Camera = 0, 1
say: 2 brings the group back, and 2 again quickly moves the camera to it.
stop
say: A right-click with something selected raises Commanded, with what's under the mouse and what's selected, for the game's script to send them there. The keys are input actions, so Game, Controls rebinds them, and players can too.
